Benjamin Lewis wrote:
> 
> "Magic" is merely a word we use to describe something that we cannot yet
> explain using current scientific theories. 

That is the way I see it in RL; but it's a view from our scientific
perspective, no generally valid view; there are people thinking differently
about it. (Who am I to insist they are wrong.)

> In the NetHack world, many
> things fit neatly into the "magic vs. non-magic" model, but as with any
> imperfect model, there are exceptions.

Hmm.., I'm really not sure about that. In my view NH is full of exceptions,
but that's of course a matter of personal view. There is some technical
distinction between magical items and non-magical items; but that also does
not fit very well with the "RL-magic" vs. RL-non-magic model.

Ordinary sacks are physical, but you can stash arbitrary amounts of items
in these? Being hit with physical means (like swords) down near 1 HP and
recover quickly without traces? Pronounce a formular blind and the scroll
in your inventory vanishes, but does not vanish when in a sack? Stones
that influence your luck? A beartrap that reactivates after you left it?
(Just to name a few cases that make me doubt.)

I think it's hard to draw a line.

O.k., you said "_many_ things fit neatly", and that's right.(*) But,
IMO, there are also *many* things that don't fit neatly in that model.

